{%- comment -%}
  Snippet: siwa-catalog-badge | Owner: A-02 | Task: ST-03

  E-02 BadgeStamp, and the single enforcement point for USF-06 / non-negotiable
  1: ORIGINAL or IMPRESSION on every thumbnail and in the first line of every
  PDP. Every surface that shows a product asks this snippet, so there is one
  place where the answer can be wrong and one place to fix it.

  THE RESOLUTION ORDER IS THE WHOLE POINT, AND IT STOPS WHERE IT STOPS.
    1. The metafield named by the `catalog_metafield` global — merchant-owned
       structured data, the only source that is meant to carry this fact.
    2. The tags named by the `tag_original` / `tag_impression` globals, for the
       products that predate the metafield.
    3. Nothing. If `require_catalog_badge` is on, an untagged product gets a
       loud, unmissable warning stamp instead of silence, so the defect is
       caught by whoever opens the page rather than by a customer. If it is
       off, the badge is simply absent.

  THERE IS NO FOURTH STEP, AND THE VENDOR FIELD IS NOT ONE.
  The store currently keeps the dupe reference in Shopify's `vendor` field.
  That is the data defect the audit flagged, not a signal: a product whose
  vendor names another house is not thereby an Impression, and encoding that
  guess here would make the theme quietly launder a broken import into a
  catalog claim. The metafield or the tag says it, or nobody does.

  The warning takes --new, the ink outline. --sale would dress a data defect
  up as a markdown, and the three catalog colours are never re-mapped. Its
  copy is a full sentence in a nowrap stamp and it will overflow its card on
  purpose — an untagged product is supposed to look broken.

  Parameters
    product   required. Blank renders nothing.
    overlay   optional boolean. Adds --overlay to position the stamp over
              media at the inline-start corner. Callers that place the badge
              in normal flow leave it off.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign badge_line = ''

  if product != blank
    assign meta_path = settings.catalog_metafield | strip
    if meta_path contains '.'
      assign meta_parts = meta_path | split: '.'
      assign meta_namespace = meta_parts[0]
      assign meta_key = meta_parts[1]
      assign catalog_line = product.metafields[meta_namespace][meta_key].value | default: '' | downcase | strip
      if catalog_line == 'original' or catalog_line == 'impression'
        assign badge_line = catalog_line
      endif
    endif

    if badge_line == blank
      assign tag_original = settings.tag_original | downcase | strip
      assign tag_impression = settings.tag_impression | downcase | strip
      for product_tag in product.tags
        assign normalised_tag = product_tag | downcase | strip
        if tag_original != blank and normalised_tag == tag_original
          assign badge_line = 'original'
          break
        endif
        if tag_impression != blank and normalised_tag == tag_impression
          assign badge_line = 'impression'
          break
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  endif

  assign overlay_class = ''
  if overlay
    assign overlay_class = ' siwa-badge--overlay'
  endif
-%}

{%- if badge_line == 'original' -%}
  <span class="siwa-badge siwa-badge--original{{ overlay_class }}">
    {{- 'catalog.original' | t -}}
  </span>
{%- elsif badge_line == 'impression' -%}
  <span class="siwa-badge siwa-badge--impression{{ overlay_class }}">
    {{- 'catalog.impression' | t -}}
  </span>
{%- elsif product != blank and settings.require_catalog_badge -%}
  <span class="siwa-badge siwa-badge--new{{ overlay_class }}">
    {{- 'catalog.untagged_warning' | t -}}
  </span>
{%- endif -%}
